{"study_id": "zk26_lgbm_defaults_20261106_haiku_v3", "search_seed": 42, "factor_id": "55df87e7925bb6a69d40873d6fcba9ef63a7312dfd8732c3a1c16f33e397bb51", "expression": "TS_CORR(DELTA(LOG($adj_close), 1.0), $volume, 48.0)", "canonical_expression": {"op": "TS_CORR", "args": [{"op": "DELTA", "args": [{"op": "LOG", "args": [{"op": "field", "args": [], "value": "adj_close"}], "value": null}, {"op": "const", "args": [], "value": 1.0}], "value": null}, {"op": "field", "args": [], "value": "volume"}, {"op": "const", "args": [], "value": 48.0}], "value": null}, "description": "Over one trading day, the rolling correlation between 5m log returns and volume marks the flow regime. Where that correlation is positive, a signed trailing 1-hour move reflects informed or speculative flow and persists over the next 12 bars. Where it is zero or negative, the same move reflects liquidity-driven flow and partly reverses. The sign of the co-movement state, not the volume magnitude, sets the sign of short-horizon predictability. This is a different state variable from the volume-to-baseline surge tested in trials 15 to 32 and from the peer-relative surge in trial 112.", "direction": 1, "origins": [{"source": "v3_async", "trial": 158, "attempt": 158, "run_id": "futures_kernel_5m_full-all-fold2-v3_async-42-61c42b9f7c"}]}
{"study_id": "zk26_lgbm_defaults_20261106_haiku_v3", "search_seed": 42, "factor_id": "282c667b85f9e0f98fd5a7f97eca4697d9c2778027f36b27922867971f5acf1f", "expression": "CS_DEMEAN($zk_cv)", "canonical_expression": {"op": "CS_DEMEAN", "args": [{"op": "field", "args": [], "value": "zk_cv"}], "value": null}, "description": "Cross-sectionally demeaned monthly zk_cv, the trailing 12-month ratio of daily return variance to mean return, predicts the next 12 five-minute adj_close log returns with a negative sign. Products whose trailing returns are noise-dominated relative to their mean underperform same-timestamp peers. Demeaning removes common regime effects, so the test isolates product-specific monthly state. The effect should not be trailing momentum, which is checked with a same-row zk_mom12 control. The raw zk_cv form is already an admitted run member with near-zero IC, so the demeaned form must add cross-sectional information beyond it to be useful.", "direction": 1, "origins": [{"source": "v3_async", "trial": 170, "attempt": 170, "run_id": "futures_kernel_5m_full-all-fold2-v3_async-42-61c42b9f7c"}]}
{"study_id": "zk26_lgbm_defaults_20261106_haiku_v3", "search_seed": 42, "factor_id": "2bef6366cabe4d332993df3fe56d83b3b3389c69c9459ce4f9a8e6e51fb06c72", "expression": "DELTA(LOG($adj_close@1d), 60.0)", "canonical_expression": {"op": "DELTA", "args": [{"op": "LOG", "args": [{"op": "field", "args": [], "value": "adj_close@1d"}], "value": null}, {"op": "const", "args": [], "value": 60.0}], "value": null}, "description": "Over the past 60 completed daily sessions, the correlation between daily adj_close log returns and daily volume marks a persistent flow regime. When this correlation is positive, the regime carries into the next 12 five-minute log returns with a positive sign, consistent with the admitted intraday state (trial 158). Because the state is measured over months, it should add information beyond the signed 60-session cumulative return (trend control).", "direction": -1, "origins": [{"source": "v3_async", "trial": 183, "attempt": 183, "run_id": "futures_kernel_5m_full-all-fold2-v3_async-42-61c42b9f7c"}]}
{"study_id": "zk26_lgbm_defaults_20261106_haiku_v3", "search_seed": 42, "factor_id": "8a0cadfc0b2ef866c51aea279a276f4f55686d9004607abe271a42e383ad9091", "expression": "CS_DEMEAN(DELTA(LOG($adj_close@1d), 40.0))", "canonical_expression": {"op": "CS_DEMEAN", "args": [{"op": "DELTA", "args": [{"op": "LOG", "args": [{"op": "field", "args": [], "value": "adj_close@1d"}], "value": null}, {"op": "const", "args": [], "value": 40.0}], "value": null}], "value": null}, "description": "A product's forty-session daily log return splits into an idiosyncratic component, CS_DEMEAN(r40), and a common component, r40 minus CS_DEMEAN(r40), which equals the same-timestamp cross-sectional mean of r40. The idiosyncratic arm should carry a negative raw sign because product-specific overextension unwinds, and the common arm should carry a positive raw sign because shared shocks persist. Both arms predict the next 12 five-minute log returns of unsuffixed adj_close, lagged one session as in trial 161. Same-sign arms, or an r40 control that matches the common arm on both splits, refute the decomposition at this span.", "direction": -1, "origins": [{"source": "v3_async", "trial": 185, "attempt": 185, "run_id": "futures_kernel_5m_full-all-fold2-v3_async-42-61c42b9f7c"}]}
{"study_id": "zk26_lgbm_defaults_20261106_haiku_v3", "search_seed": 42, "factor_id": "885bb9b81171045872d01a6644ac7de758fe019ab9e8e54c8e25c65d45da6745", "expression": "DELTA(LOG($adj_close@1d), 20.0)", "canonical_expression": {"op": "DELTA", "args": [{"op": "LOG", "args": [{"op": "field", "args": [], "value": "adj_close@1d"}], "value": null}, {"op": "const", "args": [], "value": 20.0}], "value": null}, "description": "Futures products that share macro drivers price common shocks at different speeds. A product whose 20-completed-session log return trails its product-panel peers still carries an unpriced information gap, which closes over the following hour. The peer-demeaned 20-session relative return should therefore have a negative raw IC with the next 12 five-minute log returns. The hypothesis is refuted if the raw train and validation signs differ, if the raw 20-session trend control is within 0.002 of the primary on either split, if the one-session relative control is at least as large as the primary on both splits, or if the primary is positive on both splits.", "direction": -1, "origins": [{"source": "v3_async", "trial": 199, "attempt": 199, "run_id": "futures_kernel_5m_full-all-fold2-v3_async-42-61c42b9f7c"}]}
{"study_id": "zk26_lgbm_defaults_20261106_haiku_v3", "search_seed": 42, "factor_id": "c210f42cc194163bf6792142a4ba86c0b0b3ff09837bfdc8dbd26aab7639eb03", "expression": "DELTA(LOG($adj_close@1d), 120.0)", "canonical_expression": {"op": "DELTA", "args": [{"op": "LOG", "args": [{"op": "field", "args": [], "value": "adj_close@1d"}], "value": null}, {"op": "const", "args": [], "value": 120.0}], "value": null}, "description": "A product whose previous completed session close sits far above the trailing 120-session volume-weighted average price, the holder cost basis, faces supply overhang. Its 12-bar forward 5m adj_close log return should be negatively related to that overhang. The overhang should carry information beyond the signed 120-session return and beyond the one-session VWAP deviation tested in trials 3, 9 and 18.", "direction": -1, "origins": [{"source": "v3_async", "trial": 212, "attempt": 212, "run_id": "futures_kernel_5m_full-all-fold2-v3_async-42-61c42b9f7c"}]}
{"study_id": "zk26_lgbm_defaults_20261106_haiku_v3", "search_seed": 42, "factor_id": "585bef1a8734d8d3468622e90ea103c4611f33bede43c983edb93badd565fe17", "expression": "IF_THEN_ELSE(GT(CS_DEMEAN($zk_var), 0.0), CS_DEMEAN($zk_mom12), 0.0)", "canonical_expression": {"op": "IF_THEN_ELSE", "args": [{"op": "GT", "args": [{"op": "CS_DEMEAN", "args": [{"op": "field", "args": [], "value": "zk_var"}], "value": null}, {"op": "const", "args": [], "value": 0.0}], "value": null}, {"op": "CS_DEMEAN", "args": [{"op": "field", "args": [], "value": "zk_mom12"}], "value": null}, {"op": "const", "args": [], "value": 0.0}], "value": null}, "description": "Volatility state gates cross-sectional twelve-month momentum. Among products whose volatility (zk_var) is above their same-timestamp peers, a relative twelve-month winner (high CS_DEMEAN zk_mom12) is exposed to crash risk. Volatility-targeting holders de-risk, so its next-hour return is lower. In calmer products the same winner continues through trend-following flow. The ungated term averages these states. Correction to the Explorer premise: trials 206 and 207 did not flip sign. Their train and val_raw signs agree (trial 206: train -0.0074, val_raw -0.0077; trial 207: train -0.0142, val_raw -0.0141). The test is therefore whether a high-volatility-gated term has a larger, stable negative raw IC than the ungated term, not whether a flip is repaired. The Explorer primary, MULTIPLY(CS_DEMEAN($zk_mom12), CS_DEMEAN($zk_var)), is symmetric: it is positive in both high-high and low-low states, so a negative result would not isolate the high-volatility winner state. Attempt B adds a one-sided high-volatility gate that matches the stated mechanism.", "direction": -1, "origins": [{"source": "v3_async", "trial": 238, "attempt": 238, "run_id": "futures_kernel_5m_full-all-fold2-v3_async-42-61c42b9f7c"}]}
{"study_id": "zk26_lgbm_defaults_20261106_haiku_v3", "search_seed": 42, "factor_id": "254568c82d913fbf50b4869be9c8ee03bd37bd1607efccf8498d5f4c1a8be3d1", "expression": "DIVIDE(SUBTRACT(MAX(SUBTRACT($adj_close, $adj_high@1d), 0.0), MAX(SUBTRACT($adj_low@1d, $adj_close), 0.0)), SUBTRACT($adj_high@1d, $adj_low@1d))", "canonical_expression": {"op": "DIVIDE", "args": [{"op": "SUBTRACT", "args": [{"op": "MAX", "args": [{"op": "SUBTRACT", "args": [{"op": "field", "args": [], "value": "adj_close"}, {"op": "field", "args": [], "value": "adj_high@1d"}], "value": null}, {"op": "const", "args": [], "value": 0.0}], "value": null}, {"op": "MAX", "args": [{"op": "SUBTRACT", "args": [{"op": "field", "args": [], "value": "adj_low@1d"}, {"op": "field", "args": [], "value": "adj_close"}], "value": null}, {"op": "const", "args": [], "value": 0.0}], "value": null}], "value": null}, {"op": "SUBTRACT", "args": [{"op": "field", "args": [], "value": "adj_high@1d"}, {"op": "field", "args": [], "value": "adj_low@1d"}], "value": null}], "value": null}, "description": "A 5m close beyond the prior completed session's high or low, measured as signed distance outside that fixed daily band and normalized by the band width, predicts the next 12 five-minute adj_close log returns in the break direction. Stop and breakout orders cluster at these fixed reference prices, so a close beyond the prior-session extreme draws momentum-chasing flow that continues over the next hour. A failed break, where price returns inside the band, is not scored by this primary. The signed distance from a fixed daily level differs from the rolling 240-bar extreme tested in region 9fc2 (trials 45, 52, 57, 64, 67).", "direction": 1, "origins": [{"source": "v3_async", "trial": 243, "attempt": 243, "run_id": "futures_kernel_5m_full-all-fold2-v3_async-42-61c42b9f7c"}]}
